$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure B (synthesis of
carbamate-containing electrophiles). Dry Et2O (180 mL) and 2,6-lutidine
(20 mmol) were added to a dry flask charged with the secondary amine (18
mmol). The reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C, and then the
chloroformate (18 mmol) was added. The mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature, and it was stirred overnight. Next, the reaction was
quenched by the addition of aqueous HCl (1 M; 70 mL). The organic layer
was separated, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated. The product was
purified by column chromatography.
(1S,2R,5S)-2-Isopropyl-5-methylcyclohexyl 2-bromopropyl(phenyl)carbamate.
The title compound was synthesized from N-(2-bromobutyl)aniline (1.34 g,
6.1 mmol) and (S)-menthyl chloroformate (97% ee; 1.33 mL, 6.1 mmol).
Purification by chromatography (5% → 100% Et2O/hexanes) yielded 2.18 g
(88%) of a light-yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.36-7.32 (m, 2H),
7.25-7.20 (m, 3H), 4.58 (br s, 1H), 4.12-3.86 (m, 3H), 2.04 (br s, 1H),
1.79-1.44 (m, 7H), 1.02-0.73 (m, 13H) [mixture of diastereomers]. 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 155.4, 141.5, 128.9, 127.5, 126.8, 76.1, 57.6, 47.0, 46.5,
46.4, 41.1, 34.2, 31.3, 26.29, 26.27, 23.4, 23.2, 22.0, 20.7, 16.4
[mixture of diastereomers]. FT-IR (film) 2956, 2870, 1703, 1598, 1496,
1454, 1397, 1276, 1196, 1148, 1013, 966, 836, 766, 699 cm-1. MS (ESI)
[M+H]+ calcd for C20H31BrNO2: 396.1533, found: 396.1553.
