$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of Ureas 4
To a solution of 3 (1.10 g, 3.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL), amine (10
equiv), and 4-DMAP (10 equiv) were added and the mixture was stirred in
the dark overnight at r.t. It was then washed with 3% HCl and 3% NaHCO3
solution, extracted with CH2Cl2, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was crystallized from CHCl3 to get pure compound 4.
Compound 4b, yield 87%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Light-sensitive protecting groups for amines and alcohols: the
photosolvolysis of N-substituted 7-nitroindolines
