$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the reaction of
azetidines with chloroformates. A solution of azetidine (1 mmol) in
dichloromethane (4 mL) was treated with chloroformate (1.5 eq.) and
stirred at rt overnight. The crude reaction mixture was next concentrated
under reduced pressure and purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel. When the reaction was too slugish in dichloromethane
(compounds 13n-13r'), the reaction was run in refluxing acetonitrile.
(1S,2S,3R)-Methyl
(3-chloro-1-methyl-4-oxo-2,4-diphenylbutyl)-N-methyl-carbamate (13e).
Starting from azetidine 12e.S3 Yield: 87 %. Colorless oil; [α]D 20: -34
(c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6, 343K): δ 7.98-8.01 (m, 2H),
7.69 (tt, J = 1.3, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (tt, J = 1.0, 6.7 Hz, 2H), 7.37-7.39
(m, 4H), 7.26-7.34 (m, 1H), 5.83 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 4.43-4.53 (m, 1H),
3.77 (app. t, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 3.09 (s, 3H), 2.46 (s, 3H), 0.81 (d, J =
6.7 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6, 343K): δ 190.9, 156.0, 139.2,
134.2, 133.6, 129.0, 128.6, 128.3, 127.2, 58.9 and 58.8 (rotamers), 55.2,
51.9, 51.8, 30.4, 16.5; ESIMS (positive mode): 392.5, 324.5; HRMS (CI,
NH3) m/z calcd. for C20H23ClNO3 [M+H]+ 360.1366, found 360.1373.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of azetidines with chloroformates
