$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Ketocarbamates 1. In a drybox, imine (0.48 mmol) and chloroformate (1.91
mmol) were dissolved in acetonitrile (10 mL) then the solution was
stirred for 15 min in a 50 mL reaction bomb. To this solution was added
Pd2dba3•CHCl3 (25 mg, 0.024 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 30 min
until the Pd2dba3•CHCl3 was dissolved. Tetrabutylammonium bromide (186
mg, 0.576 mmol) in methylene chloride (5 mL) and the organostannane (0.53
mmol) in methylene chloride (5 mL) were added to the reaction mixture.
The solution was frozen in liquid nitrogen then degassed, and carbon
monoxide (15 psi) was added. The mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 24 h. After the reaction period was completed, solvents were removed
in vacuo. The product was dissolved in 50 mL of ethyl acetate, then 25 mL
of saturated KF solution was added and the mixture was stirred for 5 h.
This solution was filtered over celite and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 X 50 mL). The organic layers were combined and dried over MgSO4 then
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure and the product was
purified by silica gel chromatography with hexane:ethylacetate as eluent.
(4-Methoxy-phenyl)-(2-oxo-2-phenyl-1-p-tolyl-ethyl)-carbamic acid benzyl
ester (entry 5) Yield: 87% 1HNMR (400MHz, CDCl3, 60 °C): δ 7.93-7.91 (d,
2H), 7.43-7.41 (t, 1H), 7.34-7.30 (t, 2H), 7.28-7.22 (m, 3H), 7.18-7.16
(m, 2H), 7.10-7.08 (d, 2H), 6.98-6.92 (q, 4H), 6.90 (br, 1H), 6.67-6.64
(d, 2H), 5.16-5.12 (d, 2H), 3.69 (s, 3H), 2.2 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125MHz,
CDCl3, 60 °C): δ 196.9, 158.6, 138.3, 137.0, 136.2, 132.9, 131.9, 130.9,
129.5, 129.3, 129.1, 128.9, 128.6, 128.4, 128.3, 127.8, 127.4, 113.6,
68.1, 67.5, 55.4, 21.1. IR (KBr): νCO: 1703 cm-1, 1691 cm-1 HRMS.
Calculated for C30H28NO4 +: 466.2013 found: 466.2012
