$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1-Cyclohexyl-3-p-tolylurea
(6h), yield 87%. mp 201 °C. Rf = 0.43 (EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR
(KBr): 3334, 3280, 3095, 3029, 2923, 2848, 1627, 1591, 1512, 1313, 651
cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 1.08-1.36 (m, 6H), 1.51-1.80 (m, 4H),
2.20 (s, 3H), 3.36-3.43 (m, 1H), 5.98 (d, NH, J = 7.6 Hz, D2O
exchangeable), 7.00 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.23 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 8.15
(bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 20.74, 24.82,
25.71, 33.48, 47.99, 118.01, 129.48, 129.98, 138.46, 154.94. Elemental
analysis calcd. for C14H20N2O: C, 72.38; H, 8.68; N, 12.06. C, 72.40; H,
8.70; N, 12.07.
