$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of benzylchloroformate (1.0 equiv)
and Amberlyst-15 (20 mg/mmol) was stirred for 5 min and amine (1.0 equiv)
was added into it. After stirring for the specified time (Table 1) at rt,
the reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate and filtered through
ordinary filter paper. The catalyst was washed thoroughly with ethyl
acetate and the filtrate was concentrated. The resulting crude was
purified by column chromatography to get the pure N-benzyloxycarbonyl
derivative. Table 3. Cbz protection of amines via Scheme 1a Entry 1
N-Cbz-3-(1,3-dioxolan-2-yl)aniline (Entry 14). 85% yield. IR (CHCl3):
3434, 3154, 3019, 2979, 2928, 1734, 1601, 1473, 1383, 1215, 1096, 910
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.97 (m, 2H), 4.04 (m, 2H), 5.13 (s,
2H), 5.71 (s, 1H), 6.64 (br s, 1H), 7.07-7.41 (m, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 65.30, 65.41, 67.05, 103.3, 121.6, 127.00, 127.68, 128.31,
128.39, 128.58, 128.64, 129.20, 135.98, 137.89, 139.05, 158.90.
Calculated elemental analysis for C17H17NO4: C, 68.21; H, 5.72; N, 4.68.
Found: C, 68.16; H, 5.63; N, 4.77.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry (environmentally friendly process),
green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-solvent, Amberlyst in H+ form
used, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Amberlyst-15-catalyzed Cbz protection of amines under solvent-free
conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
