$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-2-(2-But-2-enoyl-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-pyrido[3,4-b]indol-1-yl)acetaldehyde
(11). tert-Butyldimethyl(vinyloxy)silane (10) (3.17 g, 20 mmol) and
trans-crotonyl chloride (1.36 g, 1.25 mL, 13 mmol) were added to a
solution of β-dihydrocarboline 7 (1.70 g, 10 mmol) in THF (30 mL) at -78
°C, and the reaction was stirred for 10 min. The bath was removed, and
the reaction stirred at room temperature for 75 min, whereupon saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (60 mL) and EtOAc (60 mL) were added. The layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2 × 60 mL).
The combined organic layers were washed with H2O (60 mL) and brine (60
mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography eluting
with hexanes/EtOAc (4 : 1). 2.40 g (85%) of 11 as a pale yellow oil.
