$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-Cbz protected amines 7a-d. General Procedure. Hydrogen
chloride (5.0 eq, 4M in 1,4-dioxane) was added at room temperature over a
solution of sulfinamine V (1.0 eq) in MeOH (0.1M). After 30 minutes the
deprotection was completed and the solution was concentrated to dryness,
the amine hydrochloride was taken up in 1,4-dioxane (0.1M) and K2CO3 50 %
water solution (2.0 eq) and benzyl chloroformate (2.5 eq) were added
consecutively. The solution was stirred for 30 minutes at room
temperature and concentrated under vacuum. The mixture was poured into a
separatory funnel over water and extracted with dichloromethane. The
combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, concentrated under vacuum and purified by means of flash
chromatography on silica gel using hexane:diisopropyl ether 6:1 as
eluent. (1R)-N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-1-isopropyl-4-pentenamine (7a) Amine 7a
was synthesized following the general procedure described above starting
from 68 mg of sulfinamine Va (0.296 mmol) to afford 66 mg of a white
solid (85% yield). M.p.: 61-63 ºC. [α]25 D= +2.5 (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.87 (3H, d, J= 6.8 Hz), 0.91 (3H, d, J= 6.8 Hz),
1.31-1.44 (1H, m), 1.53-1.65 (1H, m), 1.69- 1.80 (1H, m), 2.02-2.18 (2H,
m), 3.50- 3.59 (1H, m), 4.55 (1H, d, J= 9.6 Hz), 4.94-4.98 (2H, m), 5.10
(2H, s), 5.81 (1H, ddt, J1 = 16.9 Hz, J2 = 10.2 Hz, J3 = 6.6 Hz), 7.35
(5H, m). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 17.5, 19.1, 30.5, 31.8, 32.0, 55.9,
66.5, 114.8, 128.0, 128.5, 136.7, 138.1, 156.3. HRMS (EI) calc. for
C16H23NO2 [M+]: 261.1729. Found: 261.1704.
