$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 2 for the Preparation of
Ureas from Carbamates: 1-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenethyl)-3-ethylurea 9: Into a
flame-dried 10 mL CEM microwave reaction vessel was added 4-methyl-2-
hydroxyquinoline (MeHYQ) (32 mg, 0.20 mmol), 3,4- dimethoxyphenethylamine
(171 μL, 1.00 mmol), and Nethylurethane (133 μL, 1.10 mmol). To this
mixture was added Zr(Ot-Bu)4 (40 μL, 0.10 mmol). The reaction was
incubated in CEM single mode microwave reactor (Explorer/Discover model)
with the dynamic cooling system (PowerMax®) on at 120 °C for 15 min
(maximum ramp time: 10 min, maximum power: 300 W). The reaction was
quenched by addition of MeOH (2 mL) and CH2Cl2 (2 mL). The mixture was
concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(CH2Cl2: MeOH= 15: 1) to afford urea 9 as a yellow solid (238 mg, 94%
yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Carbamates and Ureas Using Zr(IV)-Catalyzed Exchange
Processes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Chong; Porco, John A. Jr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(8), 1517-1520

