$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
trimethylene bisacylcarbamodithioates 5 To a stirred solution of 0.30 g
NH4SCN (4 mmol) in 20 cm3 MeCN was added 4 mmol acid chloride 1. The
mixture was stirred at rt for 30 min. Then, 2 mmol 1,3-propanedithiol
(2c) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h at rt. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified
by column chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane-EtOAc 2:1) to afford the pure
title compounds. Trimethylene bis(2-fluorobenzoyl)carbamodithioate (5a)
Trimethylene bis(4-methoxybenzoyl)carbamodithioate (5e) Yellow powder;
yield: 0.83 g (84%). Molecular formula: C21H22N2O4S4; Rf : 0.62; mp
178-180 °C; IR (KBr): ν = 3430 (NH), 1700, 1731 (C=O), 1151 (C=S) cm-1;
EI-MS: m/z (%) = 494 (M+, 5), 359 (39), 301 (50), 166 (57), 135 (100),
108 (61), 58 (46); 1H NMR: δ = 2.31 (qui, 3 J HH = 7.5 Hz, CH2), 3.59 (t,
3 J HH = 7.5 Hz, 2 CH2S), 3.73 (s, 2 MeO), 7.32 (d, 3 J HH = 8.5 Hz, 4 CH
arom), 7.79 (d, 3 J HH = 8.5 Hz, 4 CH arom), 10.06 (s, 2 NH) ppm; 13C
NMR: δ = 23.9 (CH2), 31.9 (2 CH2S), 54.3 (2 MeO); 128.1 (4 CH arom),
131.4 (4 CH arom), 146.3 (2 C), 164.7 (2 C=O), 204.5 (2 C=S) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product depends on stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A one-pot synthesis of alkyl acylcarbamodithioates from acid chlorides,
thiols, and ammonium thiocyanate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yavari, Issa; Iravani, Nasir; Sayyed-Alangi, S. Zahra; Hajinasiri,
Rahimeh
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Monatshefte fuer Chemie (2009), 140(10), 1199-1204

