$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Symmetric Ureas 7 A mixture of THF (30 mL), compound 3 (0.7 mmol), and
amine 4 (1.4 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared (TLC
monitoring). After adding DMAP (1.4 mmol), the mixture was then refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared (TLC monitoring). After evaporating the
solvent, the product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography
(2.5 × 7-11 cm, EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1,3-Bis(4-methoxyphenyl)urea
(7d), yield 84%. mp 238 °C (lit.18 240-241 °C). Rf = 0.18 (EtOAc /
n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3329, 3295, 2958, 2836, 1645, 1610, 1561,
1532, 1511, 1314, 1242, 1172, 1030, 827, 651, 527 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
DMSO-d6): δ 3.71 (s, 6H), 6.85 (d, 4H, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.34 (d, 4H, J = 9.0
Hz), 8.36 (bs, NH2, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ
55.61, 114.42, 120.39, 133.40, 153.42, 154.81. Elemental analysis calcd.
for C15H16N2O3: C, 66.16; H, 5.92; N, 10.29. Found: C, 66.19; H, 5.94; N,
10.31.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM CAS# 932-22-9 recovered (100%, reusable)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phenyl 4,5-dichloro-6-oxopyridazine-1(6H)-carboxylate as carbonyl source:
facile and selective synthesis of carbamates and ureas under mild
conditions
