$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Acetyl-(1-ferrocenylethyl)amine (8) Acetyl chloride (0.1 ml, 1.3 mmol)
was dropwise added to a cold solution (0 °C) of amine 7 (100 mg, 0.32
mmol) and NEt3 (0.27 ml, 1.95 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (10 ml). After 20
minutes of stirring and cooling, reaction mixture was poured into water
and extracted thrice with dichloromethane. The organic extracts were
combined, washed with water, saturated solution of NaCl, dried over
Na2SO4 and evaporated in vacuo to dryness. TLC-purification of raw
product with CH2Cl2/ EtOAc (10 : 1). 73 mg (84%) of N-Ac derivative 8 in
form of orange crystals Mp: 126–129 °C. IR (CH2Cl2) νmax/cm−1:
3433m(N–H), 1668 s (C=O, COCH3). 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ/ppm: 5.28 (s, 1H, NH),
4.81 (s, 1H, CH), 4.23 (m, 9H, Fc-H), 1.95 (s, 3H, COCH3), 1.45 (d, 3H,
CH3,3J = 4.2 Hz). 13C-NMR, APT (CDCl3) δ/ppm: 168.31 (COCH3), 91.81 (C-1,
Fc), 69.10 (Cpunsubst.), 68.49 (C-3, Fc), 68.27 (C-4, Fc), 68.01 (C-2,
Fc), 66.12 (C-5, Fc), 43.54 (CHCH3), 23.42 (COCH3), 20.46 (CHCH3). HR-MS:
calc. forC14H17NOFe = 271.134, found: 271.0658. MS (EI): m/z = 271 (100)
[M]+, 206 (70) [M+−Cp], 177 (35) [CpFe+NHAc], 147 (23) [CpFeCHMe], 120
(20) [CpFe]. Crystallographic data: C14H17FeNO, Formula (wt./g mol−1)
271.14, Crystal dimensions/mm 0.13x0.12x0.08, Space group P21/a, a (Å)
9.7917(3), b (Å) 9.3524(2), c (Å) 14.2316(6), α (°) 90, β (°) 101.995(3),
γ (°) 90.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and structure of N-substituted (1-ferrocenylethyl)amine
derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cakic Semencic, Mojca; Dropucic, Maja; Barisic, Lidija; Molcanov,
Kresimir; Rapic, Vladimir
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Structural Chemistry (2007), 18(3), 273-278

