$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Triethylamine (0.53 mL, 3.8 mmol) and methyl chloroformate (245 μL, 1.87
mmol) were added sequentially to a suspension of S6.HBF4 (508 mg, 1.51
mmol) in CH2Cl2 at 0 °C (15 mL). The reaction mixture was warmed to room
temperature overnight with stirring. Ether (30 mL) was added and the
resulting suspension was washed with water (2 × 20 mL) and brine (20 mL),
dried (MgSO4), and concentrated. The oily residue was chromatographed
(SiO2; CH2Cl2) to give 2das a white solid (0.38 g, 83%). N-Allenyl
Carbamates Methyl (2,2-diphenyl-4,5-hexadienyl)carbamate(2d), yield 0.38
g, 83% TLC (CH2Cl2): Rf = 0.41. 1H NMR (55 °C , 300 MHz): δ 7.18-7.33 (m,
10 H), 4.75 (quintet, J = 7.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.49-4.53 (m, 2 H), 4.24 (br s, 1
H), 3.95 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2 H), 3.61 (s, 3 H), 2.85 (td, J = 2.2, 7.8 Hz,
2 H). 13C{1H} NMR (55 °C , 75 MHz): δ 210.2, 157.0, 145.1, 128.5, 128.3,
126.7, 85.3, 73.9, 52.2, 50.9, 48.2, 37.5. IR (neat, cm-1): 2953, 1695,
1446, 1379, 1199, 698. HRMS calcd (found) for C20H21NO2 (M+): 307.1572
(307.1569).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Gold(I)-Catalyzed Enantioselective Hydroamination of N-Allenyl Carbamates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Zhibin; Bender, Christopher F.; Widenhoefer, Ross A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(15), 2887-2889

