$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v).
1-(4-Chlorophenyl)-3-(p-tolyl)urea (6l), yield 83%. mp 298 - 300 °C.
(lit.14 298-300 °C). Rf = 0.45 ( EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr):
3300, 3172, 3134, 3035, 1636, 1617, 1594, 1561, 1490, 1396, 1237, 1095,
1012, 817, 781, 642 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 2.24 (s, 3H), 7.08
(d, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.18- 7.48 (m, 6H), 8.58 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable),
8.75 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR 75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 20.24,
118.28, 119.50, 125.07, 128.49, 129.07, 130.69, 136.82, 138.72, 152.34.
Elemental analysis calcd. for C14H13ClN2O: C, 64.49; H, 5.03; N, 10.74.
Found: C, 64.51; H, 5.07; N, 10.78.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM CAS# 932-22-9 recovered (100%, reusable)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phenyl 4,5-dichloro-6-oxopyridazine-1(6H)-carboxylate as carbonyl source:
facile and selective synthesis of carbamates and ureas under mild
conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
