$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (C) for the Synthesis of
Carbamates 20-25. Glucosamine headgroup 8 was prepared by a modified
literature procedure, starting from N-acetyl glucosamine. Compound 8 (1
equiv) was dissolved in anhydrous DCM at 0 °C. Triethyl amine (1 equiv)
was added to the reaction mixture, followed by the corresponding
chloroformate (1 equiv). The reaction was stirred for 3 to 4 h at RT, and
the reaction mixture was then diluted with DCM and washed with water and
then brine. The organic phase was dried on sodium sulfate and was
purified via column chromatography using EtOAc/hexane (1:4). Allyl
Carbamate 21, white solid, 83% yield. mp 171.0-172.0 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.46-7.53 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.39 (m, 3H), 5.92 (m, 1H), 5.55 (s,
1H), 5.32 (d, 1H, J = 17.2 Hz). 5.23 (d, 1H, J = 10.3 Hz), 5.14 (broad d,
1H, J = 8.1 Hz), 4.73 (d, 1H, J = 2.9 Hz), 4.59(d, 2H, J = 5.5 Hz), 4.27
(m, 1H), 3.93-3.99 (m, 2H), 3.72-3.82 (m, 2H), 3.56 (t, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz),
3.39 (s, 3H), 2.81 (bs, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 156.5, 137.0,
132.4, 129.2, 128.2, 126.2, 118.0, 101.9, 99.1, 81.8, 70.3, 68.8, 66.0,
62.3, 55.5, 55.3. HRMS:[M + H]+ calcd for C18H24NO7, 366.1555; found,
366.1553.
