$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the formation of
carbamates: Ethyl
(3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-4-oxo-1,2,3,4,6,7,12,12b-octahydro-indolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-2-yl(methyl)carbamate
(21{35}). Ethyl chloroformate (8.7 mg, 7.6 μL, 0.08 mmol) was added to a
solution of 1,3-amino alcohol 18 (25 mg, 0.08 mmol) and Na2CO3 (10.6 mg,
0.1 mmol) in THF/H2O (1.5 mL of a 1 : 1 mixture). Upon completion (TLC),
the reaction was partitioned between Et2O (3 mL) and H2O (3 mL), and the
layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × 3
mL), and the combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The resultant yellow oil was
purified by flash column chromatography eluting with hexanes/EtOAc (1 :
1). Ethyl
(8-(3-fluorophenyl)-3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-4-oxo-1,2,3,4,6,7,12,12b-octahydroindolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-2-yl)(methyl)carbamate
(26{5,35}). Prepared according to the representative procedure for the
formation of carbamates. Purification: hexanes/EtOAc (1 : 2). Yield: 83%
(24.5 mg brown solid); LCMS purity: 100%. Data: mp 143-144 °C; 1H NMR
(400 MHz) δ 9.45 (br s, 1 H), 7.42-7.35 (comp, 2 H), 7.26-7.22 (m, 1 H),
7.22 (dd, J = 8.4, 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.17 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.11-7.06 (m,
1 H), 7.03 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.29-5.16 (m, 1 H), 4.82 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
1 H), 4.64-4.48 (m, 1 H), 4.21-4.01 (comp, 3 H), 2.98-2.82 (m, 1 H), 2.81
(s, 3 H), 2.70-2.52 (comp, 2 H), 2.25 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.02-1.88
(comp, 2 H), 1.48-1.41 (m, 3 H), 1.29 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR (100
MHz) δ 171.2, 162.3 (J = 244 Hz), 158.0, 143.4, 136.9, 133.7, 133.0,
129.3, 125.3, 124.0, 122.1, 121.1, 116.4, 113.9, 110.7, 108.4, 65.2,
62.5, 51.6, 49.8, 49.4, 39.1, 34.1, 29.9, 23.2, 21.6, 14.6; IR (neat)
3287, 2979, 2933, 1668, 1614, 1412, 1328, 909, 783, 732 cm-1; mass
spectrum (ESI) m/z 502.2115 [C27H30N3O4FNa (M+Na) requires 502.2118].
