solution of 1,3-amino alcohol 18 (25 mg, 0.08 mmol) and Na2CO3 (10.6 mg,
0.1 mmol) in THF/H2O (1.5 mL of a 1 : 1 mixture). Upon completion (TLC),
the reaction was partitioned between Et2O (3 mL) and H2O (3 mL), and the
layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × 3
mL), and the combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The resultant yellow oil was
purified by flash column chromatography eluting with hexanes/EtOAc (1 :
1).
N-(3-(1-Hydroxyethyl)-1,2,3,4,6,7,12,12b-octahydro-indolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-2-yl)-4-methoxy-N-methylbenzamide
(22{10}). Prepared according to the representative procedure for the
formation of amides. Purification: EtOAc. Yield: 83% (28.7 mg colorless
amorphous solid).; LCMS purity: 100%. Data: 1H NMR (400 MHz) δ 8.10 (s, 1
H), 7.48 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.38-7.35 (comp, 2 H), 7.32 (dd, J = 8.0,
0.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.17-7.13 (m, 1 H), 7.12-7.08 (m, 1 H), 6.94-6.90 (comp, 2
H), 4.74 (br, 1 H), 4.36-4.30 (m, 1 H), 3.83 (s, 3 H), 3.46 (d, J = 10.4
Hz, 1 H), 3.13 (s, 3 H), 3.09-2.98 (comp, 2 H), 2.97-2.91 (m, 1 H), 2.82
(d, J = 10.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.74 (dd, J = 15.2, 3.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.63-2.49 (comp,
2 H), 2.41 (br, 1 H), 2.22 (ddd, J = 11.6, 3.6, 3.6 Hz, 1 H), 1.31 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz) δ 172.0, 160.5, 136.2, 133.8, 129.3,
128.5, 126.9, 121.7, 119.6, 118.2, 113.8, 110.9, 108.3, 73.1, 62.2, 59.4,
55.4, 53.0, 50.1, 49.9, 41.4, 32.0, 21.9, 21.5; mass spectrum (ESI) m/z
434.2438 [C26H32N3O3 (M+1) requires 434.2438].
