$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triethylamine (0.53 mL, 3.8 mmol) and methyl
chloroformate (245 μL, 1.87 mmol) were added sequentially to a suspension
of S6.HBF4 (508 mg, 1.51 mmol) in CH2Cl2 at 0 °C (15 mL). The reaction
mixture was warmed to room temperature overnight with stirring. Ether (30
mL) was added and the resulting suspension was washed with water (2 × 20
mL) and brine (20 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated. The oily residue
was chromatographed (SiO2; CH2Cl2) to give 2das a white solid (0.38 g,
83%). 2,2,2-Trichloroethyl (2,2-diphenyl-4,5-hexadienyl)carbamate(2b)
were synthesized from S7.HBF4 using a procedure similar to that used to
synthesize 2d, For 2b:Colorless oil, 83%. TLC (EtOAc-hexanes = 1:10): Rf
= 0.33. 1H NMR (55 °C , 300 MHz): δ 7.18-7.34 (m, 10 H), 4.7 3 (quintet,
J = 7.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.67 (s, 3 H), 4.01 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2 H), 2.83-2.89 (m,
2 H). 13C{1H} NMR (55 °C , 126 MHz): δ 210.3, 154.7, 144.9, 128.6, 128.3,
126.9, 95.9, 85.3, 74.8, 74.1, 51.0, 48.4, 37.6. IR (neat, cm-1): 2883,
1718, 1407, 1351, 1113, 697. HRMS calcd (found) for C21H20Cl3NO2 (M+):
423.0560 (423.0556).
