$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
aromatic Alloc-, CBz-, Troc-carbamates To a solution of sodium azide
(0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150 mmol), and
carboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was added the
chloroformate reagent (1.10mmol) (Allylchloroformate: 120 μL,
benzylchloroformate: 150 μL, or 2,2,2 trichloroethylchloroformate:112
μL). Then the resulting mixture was stirred at 75 °C (85 °C for Troc
derivatives). When the reaction is completed by GC analysis, the mixture
was diluted with dichloromethane and a preabsorptionon silica was made.
The crude carbamate was then purified by flash chromatography onsilica
gel. Allyl 2-chloro-5-(methylthio)phenylcarbamate (27). The title
compound was prepared from2-chloro-5-(methylthio) benzoic acid (203 mg,
1.00 mmol) according to the general procedure. The desired carbamate 27
(211 mg, 82%) was obtained as a colorless oil after flash chromatography
(10%EtOAc/hexanes). Rf 0.50 (20% EtOAc/hexanes); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 8.14 (s (br), 1H), 7.24-7.21 (m, 2H), 6.87 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 6.04-5.95
(m, 1H), 5.40 (d, J = 17 Hz, 1H), 5.30 (d, J = 10 Hz, 1H), 4.70 (d, J = 5
Hz, 2H), 2.49 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 152.6, 138.8, 134.7,
131.9,128.8, 121.3, 118.5, 118.1, 116.6, 66.1, 15.6; IR 3413, 2922, 1739,
1577, 1516, 1407, 1272, 1209,1067, 928, 765 cm-1; HMRS (ESI) calcd for
C11H13ClNO2S [M+H]+: 258.0350. Found: 258.0351.
