$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-4-pentenamine (2a) To a suspension of LiAlH4 (1.13 g,
29.8 mmol) in Et2O (30 mL) at room temperature, 4-pentenenitrile (0.99
mL, 9.94 mmol) was added dropwise. After heating under reflux for two
hours (monitored by TLC) the mixture was allowed to reach room
temperature. Then, Na2SO4·10H2O was added to the mixture with vigorous
stirring until grey LiAlH4 salts turned into white. The suspension was
filtered off through a sort pad of Celite® and concentrated under vacuum.
The amine was dissolved in dioxane (12 mL), and 50 % aqueous solution of
K2CO3 (11.93 mmol, 3.29 mL) and benzyl chloroformate (14.91 mmol, 2.24
mL) were added consecutively. After stirring for 30 minutes at room
temperature the reaction mixture was concentrated under vacuum,
hydrolyzed with water and extracted with dichloromethane. The combined
organic layers were washed with brine and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4.
The filtrate was concentrated and purified by means of flash
chromatography on silica gel using hexane: ethyl acetate 7:1 as eluent to
afford 1.79 g of 2a as a colorless oil in 82% yield (2 steps). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.61 (2H, q, J= 7.1 Hz), 2.05-2.08 (2H, m), 3.18-3.24
(2H, m), 4.86 (1H, brs), 4.97-5.06 (2H, m), 5.09 (1H, d, J= 10.7 Hz),
5.28 (1H, d, J= 10.7 Hz), 5.80 (1H, ddt, J1 = 16.9 Hz, J2 = 10.1 Hz, J3 =
6.6 Hz), 7.37 (5H, m). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 29.0, 30.8, 32.0,
40.4, 66.5, 115.1, 128.0, 128.0, 128.4, 137.6, 156.3. HRMS (EI) calc. for
C13H17NO2 [M+]: 219.1246. Found: 219.1259.
