$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Symmetric Ureas 7 A mixture of THF (30 mL), compound 3 (0.7 mmol), and
amine 4 (1.4 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared (TLC
monitoring). After adding DMAP (1.4 mmol), the mixture was then refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared (TLC monitoring). After evaporating the
solvent, the product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography
(2.5 × 7-11 cm, EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1,3-diphenethylurea (7f),
yield 82%. mp 137 - 138 °C (lit.20 139.5-141 °C). Rf = 0.12 (EtOAc /
n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3336, 3060, 3025, 2947, 2932, 2878, 2861,
1615, 1575, 1513, 1305, 1236, 910, 746, 699 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 2.78 (t, 4H, J = 6.9 Hz), 3.39 (q, 4H, J = 6.6 Hz), 4.52 (bs,
NH2, D2O exchangeable ), 7.17-7.33 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3): δ
36.43, 41.61, 126.39, 128.57, 128.82, 139.19, 158.07. Elemental analysis
calcd. for C17H20N2O1: C, 76.09; H, 7.51; N, 10.44. Found: C, 76.12; H,
7.54; N, 10.46.
