$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the formation of
carbamates: Ethyl
(3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-4-oxo-1,2,3,4,6,7,12,12b-octahydro-indolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-2-yl(methyl)carbamate
(21{35}). Ethyl chloroformate (8.7 mg, 7.6 μL, 0.08 mmol) was added to a
solution of 1,3-amino alcohol 18 (25 mg, 0.08 mmol) and Na2CO3 (10.6 mg,
0.1 mmol) in THF/H2O (1.5 mL of a 1 : 1 mixture). Upon completion (TLC),
the reaction was partitioned between Et2O (3 mL) and H2O (3 mL), and the
layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × 3
mL), and the combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The resultant yellow oil was
purified by flash column chromatography eluting with hexanes/EtOAc (1 :
1). Ethyl
11-(benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)-3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-4-oxo-1,2,3,4,6,7,12,12b-octahydroindolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-2-yl(methyl)carbamate
(32{14,35}). Prepared according to the representative procedure for the
formation of carbamates. Purification: EtOAc. Yield: 82% (26.6 mg yellow
gum); LCMS purity: 98%. Data: 1H NMR (400 MHz) δ 8.37 (br s, 1 H), 7.50
(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.23-7.16 (comp, 2 H), 7.09-7.07 (comp, 2 H), 6.95
(d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.04 (s, 2 H), 5.09 (br, 1 H), 4.79 (dd, J = 11.2,
4.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.37 (br, 1 H), 4.10-4.02 (comp, 3 H), 3.16 (br, 1 H),
2.95-2.82 (comp, 2 H), 2.76 (s, 3 H), 2.63 (br, 1 H), 1.98-1.84 (m, 1 H),
1.65-1.63 (m, 1 H), 1.34 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3 H), 1.24 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3 H);
IR (neat) 3388, 2978, 2928, 1650, 1503, 1442, 1373, 1327, 1038, 789 cm-1;
mass spectrum (ESI) m/z 506.2280 [C28H31N3O6 (M+1) requires 506.2286].
