$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for Synthesis of
Carbamates: Method B. Preparation of carbamates 5b, 6b, 7b, S1, S4, 10b,
11b, 12b, 13b, 13c, 13f, 13g, 14b, and 14g. To a stirred solution of
aldehyde (2.10 mmol) in MeOH (10.5 mL) was added at rt a 40% MeOH
solution of MeNH2 (0.429 mL, 4.20 mmol). After 1 h at rt, NaBH4 (159 mg,
4.20 mmol) was added at 0°C and the mixture was stirred at rt for 30 min.
The reaction mixture was quenched with acetone (20 mL) at 0°C and the new
mixture was concentrated under reduced pressure. The residual white
solids were used for the next step without purification. To a stirred
solution of the residue in a mixture of 1:1:1 THF-acetone-H2O (10.0 mL)
was added at 0°C ClCO2R (3.78 mmol) or FmocOSu (1.28 g, 3.78 mmol, for
17g and S15). After 2 h at rt, saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL) was added
at 0°C and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc (10 mL x 3). The extracts
were washed with saturated aqueous NaCl (10 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel to afford carbamates 5b, 6b, 7b, S1, S4,
10b, 11b, 12b, 13b, 13c, 13f, 13g, 14b, and 14g. From
3-methoxybenzaldehyde. From 1-naphthaldehyde. Isopropyl
methyl(naphthalen-1-ylmethyl)carbamate (7b) as a colorless syrup, yield
82%. Rf = 0.40 (4:1 hexane-EtOAc); IR (neat, cm-1) 2979, 1696, 1471,
1399, 1250, 1147, 1112, 773; 1H NMR (500 MHz, (CD3)2SO, 80°C, solvent
residual peak = 2.50) δ 1.23 (6H, d, J = 6.3 Hz), 2.79 (3H, s), 4.89 (1H,
sept, J = 6.3 Hz), 4.91 (2H, s), 7.35 (1H, d, J = 7.2 Hz), 7.49 (1H, dd,
J = 8.1, 7.2 Hz), 7.51-7.58 (2H, m), 7.86 (1H, d, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.95 (1H,
m), 8.12 (1H, m); 13C NMR (125 MHz, 80°C, (CD3)2SO) δ 21.6, 33.0, 49.0,
67.7, 122.8, 124.9, 125.0, 125.4, 125.8, 127.4, 128.2, 130.8, 132.7,
133.2, 155.1; LRMS (EI) m/z (M)+ 257.1; HRMS (EI) m/z (M)+ calcd for
C16H19NO2 257.1416, found 257.1414.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Smooth Isoindolinone Formation from Isopropyl Carbamates via
Bischler-Napieralski-Type Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
