$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). 1,1-Diisopropyl-3-phenylurea
(6d), yield 82%. mp 113 °C (lit.8 112-113 °C). Rf = 0.6 (EtOAc / n-hexane
= 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3278, 3122, 3051, 2968, 2927, 2871, 1631, 1583,
1446, 1334, 1147, 746 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 1.24 (d, 12H, J
= 6.6 Hz), 3.78-3.89 (m, 2H), 6.89 (t, 1H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.19 (t, 2H, J =
7.2 Hz), 7.42 (d, 2H, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.93 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C
NMR 75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 21.66, 45.98, 120.43, 121.72, 128.51, 141.36,
154.31. Elemental analysis calcd. for C13H20N2O: C, 70.87; H, 9.15; N,
12.72. Found: C, 70.88; H, 9.17; N, 12.72.
