$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
trimethylene bisacylcarbamodithioates 5 To a stirred solution of 0.30 g
NH4SCN (4 mmol) in 20 cm3 MeCN was added 4 mmol acid chloride 1. The
mixture was stirred at rt for 30 min. Then, 2 mmol 1,3-propanedithiol
(2c) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h at rt. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified
by column chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane-EtOAc 2:1) to afford the pure
title compounds. Trimethylene bis(2-fluorobenzoyl)carbamodithioate (5a)
Trimethylene bispropionylcarbamodithioate (5f) Yellow powder; yield: 0.55
g (81%). Molecular formula: C11H18N2O2S4)); Rf : 0.78; mp 160-162 °C; IR
(KBr): ν = 3438 (NH), 1699, 1716, (C=O), 1154 (C=S) cm-1; EI-MS: m/z (%)
= 338 (M+, 4), 281 (59), 223 (52), 166 (71), 106 (30), 57 (100); 1H NMR:
δ = 1.24 (t, 3 J HH = 8.7 Hz, 2 Me), 2.43 (q, 3 J HH = 8.5 Hz, 2 CH2),
2.68 (qui, 3 J HH = 7.6 Hz, CH2), 3.38 (t, 3 J HH = 7.5 Hz, 2 CH2S), 9.49
(s, 2 NH) ppm; 13C NMR: δ = 8.9 (2 Me), 24.2 (CH2), 31.7 (2 CH2S), 35.5
(2 CH2), 170.8 (2 C=O), 203.8 (2 C=S) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product depends on stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A one-pot synthesis of alkyl acylcarbamodithioates from acid chlorides,
thiols, and ammonium thiocyanate
