$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Symmetric Ureas 7 A mixture of THF
(30 mL), compound 3 (0.7 mmol), and amine 4 (1.4 mmol) was stirred at
r.t. until compound 3 disappeared (TLC monitoring). After adding DMAP
(1.4 mmol), the mixture was then refluxed until carbamate 5 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After evaporating the solvent, the product was isolated
by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm, EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2,
v/v). 1,3-Diphenylurea (7a), yield 81%. mp 240 - 241 °C (lit.15 239-243
°C). Rf = 0.51 (EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3322, 3038, 1649,
1597, 1554, 1528, 1514, 1486, 1406, 1324, 1298, 1216, 905, 813, 756, 662
cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 6.98 (t, 2H, J = 7.4 Hz), 7.28 (t, 4H,
J = 7.8 Hz), 7.45 (d, 4H, J = 7.9 Hz), 8.65 (bs, NH2, D2O exchangeable).
13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 18.63, 122.26, 129.24, 140.16, 152.99.
Elemental analysis calcd. for C13H12N2O: C, 73.56; H, 5.70; N, 13.20.
Found: C, 73.57; H, 5.73; N, 13.22.
